          "path": "_m/d/n/k/j/clinton-tennessee-wp/clinton-ritz-hoskins-tn1.jpg",
          "filename": "Clinton-ritz-hoskins-tn1.jpg",
          "caption": "The Ritz Theater and Hoskins Drugstore in Clinton, Tennessee, in the southeastern United States.  The Ritz was built in World War II under the direction of the War Production Board, and opened in late 1945.  In the 1970s, the Ritz hosted an Opry-esque show called \"The Red Speeks Show.\"  The theater closed in 1987, but reopened in 2000.  Both the Ritz and the Hoskins Drugstore were added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1998.\n\nThe Ritz is located at 119 Main Street, across from the Anderson County Courthouse.",
          "alt": "The Ritz Theater and Hoskins Drugstore in Clinton, Tennessee, in the southeastern United States.  The Ritz was built in World War II under the direction of the War Production Board, and opened in late 1945.  In the 1970s, the Ritz hosted an Opry-esque show called \"The Red Speeks Show.\"  The theater closed in 1987, but reopened in 2000.  Both the Ritz and the Hoskins Drugstore were added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1998.\n\nThe Ritz is located at 119 Main Street, across from the Anderson County Courthouse.",
